const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先区分协议与价格",en:"Separate protocol from price"},body:{zh:"Böhme、Christin、Edelman与Moore面向非技术读者介绍比特币的设计、经济机制与治理。文章把支付协议、分布式记录和现实金融系统的连接放在一起，而不是从价格曲线出发给资产估值。",en:"Böhme, Christin, Edelman and Moore introduce Bitcoin's design, economics and governance to nontechnical readers. They connect a payment protocol and distributed records to the conventional financial system rather than deriving value from a price chart."}},{title:{zh:"签名解决授权，账本解决记录",en:"Signatures authorize; the ledger records"},body:{zh:"作者草稿将两个问题分开：数字签名帮助验证支出的授权，分布式交易记录帮助追踪输入与此前输出的联系。签名并不负责隐藏整份交易历史，也不证明现实中的法律身份。理解这一区别，才能避免把“使用密码学”直接理解成所有交易内容都被加密保密。",en:"The author draft separates authorization through digital signatures from recording transactions whose inputs refer to earlier outputs. A signature does not conceal the entire transaction history or establish a real-world legal identity. Cryptographic verification and secrecy are therefore different properties, not interchangeable descriptions of the system."},reference:{url:"https://www.benedelman.org/publications/bitcoin-15jul2014.pdf",label:{zh:"2014年作者草稿：Enabling Technologies / The Role of Cryptography",en:"2014 author draft: Enabling Technologies / The Role of Cryptography"}}},{title:{zh:"机制不能脱离参与者",en:"Mechanisms depend on participants"},body:{zh:"综述讨论交易记录、参与激励、发行路径和权力集中等问题。即使规则在协议中写明，仍然需要理解谁运行系统、谁提供中介服务，以及参与者怎样响应激励，不能把技术描述当作完整经济解释。",en:"The overview discusses transaction records, participation incentives, issuance and concentration. Protocol rules alone do not fully explain who operates the system, provides intermediation or responds to incentives."}},{title:{zh:"隐私与去中心化都有边界",en:"Privacy and decentralization have limits"},body:{zh:"作者强调灵活性、隐私和监管相关特征并非没有限制。本站建议把链上可见信息与链下身份、交易所账户和托管关系分开，避免把公开记录解释成匿名保证，或把协议特征套用到所有服务商。",en:"The authors emphasize limits to flexibility, privacy and regulatory claims. Distinguish on-chain records from off-chain identity, exchange accounts and custody. Public records do not establish anonymity or identical intermediary behavior."}},{title:{zh:"激励机制同时带来资源成本",en:"Participation incentives also consume resources"},body:{zh:"草稿把工作量证明与维护账本的激励联系起来：同一机制既提高伪造参与的成本，也奖励记录维护者，但计算活动消耗现实资源。阅读重点是激励、竞争与成本之间的关系；文中的历史奖励和能耗数字不能作为今天的参数，更不能只由交易价格判断网络运行状况。",en:"The draft links proof of work to incentives for maintaining the shared record: the mechanism makes fabricated participation costly and rewards record maintenance, while computation consumes resources. The useful reading is about incentives, competition and costs. Historical reward and energy figures are not current parameters, and exchange prices alone do not describe network operation."},reference:{url:"https://www.benedelman.org/publications/bitcoin-15jul2014.pdf",label:{zh:"2014年作者草稿：Incentives for Participation",en:"2014 author draft: Incentives for Participation"}}},{title:{zh:"再分别阅读采用模型与市场数据",en:"Then study adoption and markets"},body:{zh:"这篇提供概念背景；Tokenomics讨论平台采用与价值的模型，跨交易所研究讨论交易场所分割。三个对象相关但不能互换：交易量不是用户数，交易所价格也不是协议全部经济活动。",en:"This is conceptual background. Tokenomics models platform adoption, while cross-exchange research studies venue segmentation. Trading volume, users and protocol activity are related but not interchangeable objects."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读结合2014年作者草稿与2015年综述摘要，仅解释历史设计思路，不提供当前协议、安全、监管或投资判断。",en:"The guide combines the 2014 author draft with the 2015 overview abstract to explain historical design ideas, not current protocol, security, regulatory or investment conditions."}};export{e as default};
